   "downstream_probe": "One-arm probe (leaf-probe ablation only, per writeup-422 caveat that cross-arm top-read-shift is non-specific): ablated the leaf's 4 PCA probes (a4,a3,a2) and measured top-read shift on all 117 downstream heads (layers 5-17) at member vs off-member positions, same 24-row sample used for leaf_input_decomp. Finding: DIFFUSE, not concentrated -- mean shift 20.1% at member positions, 94.9% of downstream heads shift >10% of their top reads; off-member positions in the same rows show nearly the same disruption (mean 16.9%, 92.3%>10%). No single dominant downstream consumer emerged (top movers spread across layers 5,6,7,8,9,16,17 at similar 32-45% magnitudes, unlike a genuine courier signature e.g. courier_centrality a6.h3 which concentrates shift in a small enriched set). This adds a real (negative) lead: the leaf has no specific downstream reader any more than it has a specific upstream writer -- the causal effect (concentration 5.2) looks like it comes from removing a fairly large, generically-influential subspace rather than a localized circuit. dCE at member positions is the certified cl.sign_stats value (dce_members=0.101, abs_dce_members=0.847), not recomputed.",
