   "objection": "The record cannot rule out that concentration=5.2 is explained by member-position FRAGILITY rather than by this leaf's specific machinery: members already run high base CE (mean 5.555, only 21.3% under 3 nats), so any sufficiently large ablation of early-layer directions (not just these 4 specific PCA probes) might show similarly large dCE on these same hard positions purely because high-loss positions are more sensitive to generic perturbation. Neither leaf_input_decomp's writer-share null nor my downstream-shift check controls for this -- both show the effect is diffuse/non-localized, which is consistent with an honest negative but equally consistent with a magnitude-matched-random-subspace-on-these-same-rows control never having been run. That control (ablate a random rank-14 subspace of a2/a3/a4 restricted to the same member rows, compare concentration) would be the decisive follow-up."
